}, {"reference": {"publication_info": {"journal_volume": "69", "artid": "80", "page_start": "80", "journal_title": "Prog.Theor.Phys.Suppl."}}}, {"reference": {"publication_info": {"journal_volume": "139", "artid": "1", "page_start": "1", "journal_title": "Phys.Lett.A"}}}, {"reference": {"publication_info": {"journal_volume": "32", "artid": "2287", "page_start": "2287", "journal_title": "Int.J.Theor.Phys."}}}, {"reference": {"publication_info": {"journal_volume": "25", "artid": "397", "page_start": "397", "journal_title": "Stud.Hist.Phil.Sci."}}}, {"reference": {"publication_info": {"journal_volume": "156", "artid": "1377", "page_start": "1377", "journal_title": "Phys.Rev."}}}, {"reference": {"publication_info": {"journal_volume": "1", "artid": "566", "page_start": "566", "journal_title": "Phys.Rev.D"}}, "curated_relation": false, "record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/61859"}}, {"reference": {"publication_info": {"journal_volume": "21", "artid": "3316", "page_start": "3316", "journal_title": "Phys.Rev.D"}}, "curated_relation": false, "record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/158252"}}, {"reference": {"publication_info": {"journal_volume": "24", "artid": "359", "page_start": "359", "journal_title": "Phys.Rev.D"}}, "curated_relation": false, "record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/10248"}}, {"reference": {"publication_info": {"journal_volume": "31", "artid": "555", "page_start": "555", "journal_title": "Proc.Cambridge Phil.Soc."}}}, {"reference": {"publication_info": {"journal_volume": "2", "artid": "127", "page_start": "127", "journal_title": "Found.Phys.Lett."}}}, {"reference": {"publication_info": {"journal_volume": "52", "artid": "25", "page_start": "25", "journal_title": "Synthese"}}}, {"reference": {"publication_info": {"journal_volume": "18", "artid": "569", "page_start": "569", "journal_title": "Nous"}}}, {"reference": {"publication_info": {"journal_volume": "6", "artid": "571", "page_start": "571", "journal_title": "Found.Phys.Lett."}}, "curated_relation": false, "record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/359421"}}, {"reference": {"publication_info": {"journal_volume": "39", "artid": "3010", "page_start": "3010", "journal_title": "Phys.Rev.A"}}, "curated_relation": false, "record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/294153"}}, {"reference": {"publication_info": {"journal_volume": "1", "artid": "441", "page_start": "441", "journal_title": "EPL"}}}, {"reference": {"publication_info": {"journal_volume": "8", "artid": "105", "page_start": "105", "journal_title": "Found.Phys.Lett."}}, "curated_relation": false, "record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/376305"}}], "number_of_pages": 165, "referenced_authors_bais": ["K.Kraus.1", "T.Weber.6", "E.Deotto.1", "W.H.Zurek.1", "J.R.Ellis.1", "O.Nicrosini.1", "B.Podolsky.1", "M.Porrati.1", "F.Karolyhazy.1", "A.Bassi.2", "R.Grassi.1", "S.Goldstein.1", "D.Bohm.1", "S.P.Tomczak.1", "Y.Aharonov.1", "P.M.Pearle.1", "W.T.Strunz.1", "S.Mohanty.1", "Dimitri.V.Nanopoulos.1", "Steven.Weinberg.1", "K.E.Hellwig.1", "E.Joos.1", "S.Putterman.1", "G.Lindblad.1", "H.D.Zeh.1", "D.Z.Albert.1", "R.Omnes.1", "Adrian.Kent.1", "Hugh.Everett.1", "Nathan.Rosen.1", "K.Haller.9", "D.Deutsch.1", "N.Gisin.1", "W.F.Stinespring.1", "M.M.Buffa.1", "G.C.Ghirardi.1", "D.Durr.1", "L.Diosi.1", "E.J.Squires.1", "Nino.Zanghi.1", "A.Rimini.2", "R.B.Griffiths.1", "A.A.Komar.1", "M.Tegmark.1", "Albert.Einstein.1"], "legacy_version": "20190508164804.0", "inspire_categories": [{"term": "General Physics"}, {"term": "Quantum Physics", "source": "arxiv"}], "legacy_creation_date": "2003-04-08", "preprint_date": "2003-02", "author_count": 2, "public_notes": [{"source": "arXiv", "value": "165 pages, LaTeX"}], "first_author": {"emails": ["bassi@ictp.trieste.it"], "full_name": "Bassi, Angelo", "last_name": "Bassi", "first_name": "Angelo", "recid": 1258732}, "control_number": 616579, "dois": [{"value": "10.1016/S0370-1573(03)00103-0"}, {"material": "publication", "source": "arXiv", "value": "10.1016/S0370-1573(03)00103-0"}], "earliest_date": "2003-02", "document_type": ["article"], "texkeys": ["Bassi:2003gd"], "abstracts": [{"value": "The report presents an exhaustive review of the recent attempt to overcome the difficulties that standard quantum mechanics meets in accounting for the measurement (or macro-objectification) problem, an attempt based on the consideration of nonlinear and stochastic modifications of the Schroedinger equation. The proposed new dynamics is characterized by the feature of not contradicting any known fact about microsystems and of accounting, on the basis of a unique, universal dynamical principle, for wavepacket reduction and for the classical behavior of macroscopic systems. We recall the motivations for the new approach and we briefly review the other proposals to circumvent the above mentioned difficulties which appeared in the literature. In this way we make clear the conceptual and historical context characterizing the new approach. After having reviewed the mathematical techniques (stochastic differential calculus) which are essential for the rigorous and precise formulation of the new dynamics, we discuss in great detail its implications and we stress its relevant conceptual achievements. The new proposal requires also to work out an appropriate interpretation: a procedure which leads us to a reconsideration of many important issues about the conceptual status of theories based on a genuinely Hilbert space description of natural processes. We also discuss the possibility and the problems one meets in trying to develop an analogous formalism for the relativistic case. Finally we discuss the experimental implications of the new dynamics for various physical processes which should allow, in principle, to test it against quantum mechanics."}, {"source": "arXiv", "value": "The report presents an exhaustive review of the recent attempt to overcome the difficulties that standard quantum mechanics meets in accounting for the measurement (or macro-objectification) problem, an attempt based on the consideration of nonlinear and stochastic modifications of the Schroedinger equation. The proposed new dynamics is characterized by the feature of not contradicting any known fact about microsystems and of accounting, on the basis of a unique, universal dynamical principle, for wavepacket reduction and for the classical behavior of macroscopic systems. We recall the motivations for the new approach and we briefly review the other proposals to circumvent the above mentioned difficulties which appeared in the literature. In this way we make clear the conceptual and historical context characterizing the new approach. After having reviewed the mathematical techniques (stochastic differential calculus) which are essential for the rigorous and precise formulation of the new dynamics, we discuss in great detail its implications and we stress its relevant conceptual achievements. The new proposal requires also to work out an appropriate interpretation; a procedure which leads us to a reconsideration of many important issues about the conceptual status of theories based on a genuinely Hilbert space description of natural processes. We also discuss the possibility and the problems one meets in trying to develop an analogous formalism for the relativistic case. Finally we discuss the experimental implications of the new dynamics for various physical processes which should allow, in principle, to test it against quantum mechanics.", "abstract_source_suggest": {"input": "arXiv"}}], "refereed": true, "primary_arxiv_category": ["quant-ph"], "external_system_identifiers": [{"schema": "ADS", "value": "2003PhR...379..257B"}, {"schema": "SPIRES", "value": "SPIRES-5519560"}, {"schema": "MSNET", "value": "1979602"}], "titles": [{"title": "Dynamical reduction models"}, {"source": "arXiv", "title": "Dynamical Reduction Models"}], "publication_type": ["review"], "facet_author_name": ["1008494_Giancarlo Ghirardi", "1258732_Angelo Bassi"], "_oai": {"sets": ["Literature"], "id": "oai:inspirehep.net:616579", "updated": "2026-02-06T09:57:06.850288"}, "curated": true, "journal_title_variants": ["Phys.Rept.", "Phys. Rept."], "arxiv_eprints": [{"categories": ["quant-ph", "hep-th"], "value": "quant-ph/0302164"}]}, "links": {"bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/616579?format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/616579?format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/616579?format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/616579?format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/616579?format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/616579?format=cv", "citations": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A616579"}, "updated": "2026-02-06T09:57:06.850288+00:00", "created": "2003-04-08T00:00:00+00:00", "id": "616579"}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1016%2Fs0370-1573%2803%2900103-0&size=5&page=1", "bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1016%2Fs0370-1573%2803%2900103-0&size=5&page=1&format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1016%2Fs0370-1573%2803%2900103-0&size=5&page=1&format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1016%2Fs0370-1573%2803%2900103-0&size=5&page=1&format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1016%2Fs0370-1573%2803%2900103-0&size=5&page=1&format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1016%2Fs0370-1573%2803%2900103-0&size=5&page=1&format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1016%2Fs0370-1573%2803%2900103-0&size=5&page=1&format=cv"}}